'''VersionWatch''' tells administrators when the software behind their wiki needs updating: MediaWiki itself, PHP, the database server, and every installed extension and skin.

It is meant for wikis that are not run from a deployment pipeline, such as wikis on shared hosting, where nobody notices that an extension has a security fix waiting.

== Features ==
* '''[[Special:VersionWatch]]''' compares everything that is installed with its upstream releases and repositories.
* '''Security fixes''' are recognised by the <code>SECURITY:</code> prefix Wikimedia uses in commit messages, both for extensions and for newer MediaWiki releases, and listed first.
* Each update '''lists the changes''' it brings and links to a download: [[Special:ExtensionDistributor|ExtensionDistributor]] for Wikimedia-hosted extensions, a zip for GitHub-hosted ones.
* Changes that do not affect a wiki, such as translation updates and changes to development tools, '''do not count''' as updates.
* It '''warns''' when an update needs a newer PHP or MediaWiki than the wiki has.
* It checks whether the installed extensions and skins are '''ready for the newest MediaWiki release'''.
* Extensions bundled with MediaWiki are checked against the exact commit their release shipped.
* With [[Extension:Echo|Echo]], users with the <code>versionwatch</code> right get a '''notification''' when something newly needs attention.
* A maintenance script for cron, which only prints something when there is something to do.
* An '''API module''' for monitoring tools.

